<BaseLayout title="Asia Market Entry and Regional Expertise | Alan Yeong" description="Practical perspectives on entering and growing across Asian markets, grounded in consumer behaviour, cultural context and commercial realities."><header class="page-hero"><div class="wrap narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Asia expertise</p><h1>Asia is not one market</h1><p class="lead">Regional ambition must be grounded in country-level context, consumer behaviour and commercial reality.</p></div></header><div class="page-body wrap narrow prose"><h2>What travels—and what does not</h2><p>Strategies that work in one country may not transfer neatly to another. Even familiar consumer needs can be expressed differently because of language, history, income, social norms and local expectations.</p><h2>A decision-led lens</h2><p>I help organisations distinguish between the assumptions they can carry forward, the elements that require adaptation and the questions that still need local evidence.</p><h2>Market claims remain evidence-led</h2><p>Specific country experience and case evidence will be published only after each claim is verified and approved.</p><a class="button" href="/contact/">Discuss an Asia market question</a></div></BaseLayout>
